Verse 1:
[Bb]Rock of Ages, [Eb]cleft for [Bb]me, Let me hide my[F7]self in [Bb]Thee;
[Bb]Let the [F7]water and the [Bb]blood, From Thy [F7]riven side which [Bb]flowed,
[Bb]Be of sin the [Eb]double [Bb]cure, [Gm]Cleanse me [Bb]from its [F7]guilt and [Bb]power.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Not [Eb]the [Bb]labor [F7]of [Bb]my hands
[Bb]Can [F7]fulfill [Bb]Thy [F7]law's [Bb]demands;
[Bb][Eb]Could [Bb]my [Gm]zeal [Bb]no [F7]respite [Bb]know,
[Bb]Could [Eb]my [Bb]tears [F7]forever [Bb]flow,
[Bb]All [F7]for [Bb]sin [F7]could [Bb]not atone;
[Bb][Eb]Thou [Bb]must [Gm]save, [Bb]and [F7]Thou [Bb]alone.

Verse 3:
[Bb]When [Eb]my [Bb]pilgrimage [F7]I [Bb]close;
[Bb]Victor [F7]o'er [Bb]the [F7]last [Bb]of foes,
[Bb][Eb]When [Bb]I [Gm]soar [Bb]to [F7]worlds [Bb]unknown,
[Bb]And [Eb]behold [Bb]Thee [F7]on [Bb]Thy throne,
[Bb]Rock [F7]of [Bb]Ages, [F7]cleft [Bb]for me,
[Bb][Eb]Let [Bb]me [Gm]hide [Bb]myself [F7]in [Bb]Thee.
